# Spectrum 2 (`@react-spectrum/s2`)

## Building components

- Prefer primitives from `react-aria-components` (e.g. `Button as RACButton`) over reimplementing behavior.
- Style with the `style` macro — never ad-hoc hex/rgb or arbitrary CSS modules:

```tsx
import {style} from '../style' with {type: 'macro'};
// or from style-utils helpers colocated in the package
```

- Keep visual variants as typed props (`variant`, `fillStyle`, etc.), not free-form class strings.
- User-facing strings: `intlMessages from '../intl/*.json'` + `useLocalizedStringFormatter`.

## Patterns to preserve

- Use Spectrum context helpers already in the package (`useSpectrumContextProps`, slot contexts).
- Use `onPress` / RAC press APIs — do not add `onClick` to public Spectrum APIs.
- Colocate stories under `stories/` and tests under `test/`.

## Consumer docs

For app-facing S2 usage and the style macro token set, see `rules/react-spectrum-s2.mdc` and `rules/style-macro.mdc`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="my-btn" onClick={...} style={{color: '#ff0000'}} />

// ✅ GOOD
<RACButton className={style({...})} onPress={...}>...</RACButton>
```
